  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOTE CLIMATE ACTION</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project in Nairobi, Kajiado and Machakos Counties is led by children living with diverse disabilities, and aims to foster a greener and more sustainable environment for the future by nurturing sprouts today. This initiative will promote environmental stewardship, inclusion and empowerment of children with disabilities in climate action. By repurposing waste plastic bottles to create localized tree drip systems, working with local tree vendors, collaborating with environmental studies teachers, and incorporating an innovative IT-based tracking system, the project seeks to revolutionize climate change action and create a positive impact on the environment and the lives of the children (stewardship, inclusivity, waste plastic repurposing, indigenous tree planting, education incentives and data tracking system</narrative>
  </description>
